WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:06.740
What’s up wisecrack?

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.240
Jared here.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:12.340
Today we are talking about a colossal series
with amazing fight scenes, a shit ton of crying

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.210
cowards, and gargantuan steamy ken dolls:
Attack on Titan.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:22.310
Many anime properties explore death but few
ruminate on the visceral reality of it

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.070
quite like Attack On Titan.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:30.390
In a way, Titans are the physical personification
of death: walking reminders of human mortality—a

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:34.340
sort of existential confrontation with the
inevitability of demise.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.190
It’s pretty horrifying.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:41.160
However, the darkest element of the series
isn’t the eerily introspective confrontations

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.530
with death or the fact that Titans have no
genitals—it’s the construction of the

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.160
society behind the walls itself.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:54.040
The show is set in an anachronistic quasi-Germanic
society full of German architecture, German

00:00:54.040 --> 00:01:01.969
war cries, and characters with German names.

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:05.000
But the similarities to German history don’t
stop there.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Upon closer inspection, the political ideology
of this society lines up with the beliefs

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.970
of one of the most notorious Nazi philosophers:
Carl Schmitt.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:17.659
Now just to be clear: Schmitt’s a real piece
of shit.

00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:21.009
Dude was a card carrying Nazi, unrepentant
to the end.

00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:26.040
We are in no way saying that his ideas are
good, nor is Attack on Titan saying they're good.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.220
We are saying that the show can be understood
as an exploration of his ideas.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.390
What makes Attack on Titan so dark is that
it presents us with a society, faced with

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:39.770
a horrific enemy, that maintains stability
while reflecting Nazi ideology.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:43.380
Is Attack on Titan one of the most provocative
shows out there?

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.270
Not because of the balls to the wall violence,
but because it dares to ask: is it possible

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:53.850
that in this dystopian society—a controversial
philosophy may be the only thing keeping the

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.690
fabric of society from collapsing?

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:59.399
Welcome to this Wisecrack Edition on Attack
on Titan.

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:03.630
Spoiler alert, and oh yeah- We’re only covering
the TV show, not the manga.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:07.729
They’re going to be different anyway.

00:02:07.729 --> 00:02:11.220
Also we had to use dubs so we don’t have
subtitles all over the video.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.569
So please, don’t freak out.

00:02:13.569 --> 00:02:17.820
Central to Schmitt’s philosophy and Attack
on Titan’s civilization is the concept of

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.230
what he calls “the political.”

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.989
For Schmitt there are three concepts that
situate the political and create a stable

00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:29.849
society: conflict and inequality, clear distinctions
between friends and enemies, and sovereignty.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:34.330
The first thing that Schmitt highlights is
that conflict, division, and inequality among

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.900
human beings is inevitable.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:42.390
Central to this is an understanding that humanity,
in its most basic nature, is savage and hellish.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.740
People are essentially shitty and life isn’t
fair.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:59.040
Mikasa, Armin, and Eren, all make arguments
about the way the world is that are completely

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.670
in line with this thinking.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:05.730
When young Mikasa is kidnapped it is the image
of a mantis eating a moth and her father with

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:10.170
a duck he hunted, that kick starts the killing
spree that saves her and Eren.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:15.330
It's a constant theme that the show returns
to: it’s a dog eat dog world and you have

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.060
to fight to survive.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:26.890
This constant war against all is in line with
philosopher Thomas Hobbes’ understanding of humanity’s

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:32.150
most basic nature- we’re all monsters at
heart and social structures are the only thing

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.239
that can keep us at bay.

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:39.409
Schmitt takes things a step further: it isn’t
just that people are terrible: rather hostility

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:40.810
is unavoidable.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:46.239
For Schmitt, inequality is sort of inevitable:
people will always be smarter, fitter, more

00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:49.470
attractive, and it’s not the job of politics
to fix it.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:54.120
If society is to function properly, according
to Schmitt, it doesn’t make sense to attempt

00:03:54.120 --> 00:04:00.700
to eliminate antagonism or inequality because
they will always exist: instead a strong sovereign

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:05.261
ought to be concerned with maintaining order
and control of the population--focusing on

00:04:05.261 --> 00:04:08.989
social issues like inequality misses the point,
for him.

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:13.909
In Attack on Titan, we see this first hand:
classes are separated by literal walls.

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:16.540
Each wall section is its own caste system.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:20.700
The people in wall Maria are not as safe as
the people inside wall Rose and Sena.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:25.250
While people are being eaten in Trost—people
in the inner city are chillin in castles,

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.660
playing chess and shit.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:30.880
The scouts venture past the wall and risk
their lives while the MP’s in the inner

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.320
walls barely know how to use their Omnidirectional
Mobility Gear—they just sort of get drunk

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.240
all day.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:43.780
Most media narratives would see severe inequality
as something to be repaired, but in Attack

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:47.760
on Titan- we haven’t seen much evidence
of that. At least yet.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.940
Trying to alleviate things like inequality,
for Schmitt, is a distraction from what’s

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:56.880
really important for “the political”:nationalism
and survival—and this is where the parallels

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.040
between the series and Schmitt get pretty creepy.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:04.700
Nowhere is this focus on the nationalistic
duty of the warrior class more apparent than

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.970
in the theme song for the first half of season
1, which looks and sounds like “triumph

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.690
of the will” level nationalistic propaganda.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:17.151
The lyrics of the song are about fighting
past defeat, trampling over corpses, having

00:05:17.151 --> 00:05:22.230
the will of starving wolves and piercing scarlet
holes in the twilight with bows and arrows,

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:26.170
over scenes of the soaring military and crazy
battle scenes.

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:31.340
It may as well have been a post-World War
I rallying cry for the defeated German people.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:35.440
Which gets us to Schmitt’s second element
of the political:a clear distinction between

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.010
friend and enemy.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:42.520
The idea is—good governments need an enemy
to struggle against without completely dominating

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.520
them.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:48.000
The titans provide a sort of check against
total conquest beyond the wall.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:53.160
Without a clear enemy, human nature drives
a war against all: an unending civil war full

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:58.940
of war crimes, dehumanization, and the eradication
of your own people becomes an inevitability.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:03.750
The existence of a clear enemy impedes the
quest for constant war and infighting.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.600
Both Erwin and Pyxis are concerned with this
friend enemy distinction.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.160
On the wall with Eren, Pyxus makes this very
comment about the necessity of the Titans

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.140
as the enemy:

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:36.060
Both Pyxis and Erwin Smith worry that the
Titans aren’t the actual enemy—that they

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:42.050
are not the real threat—the real threat
is humanity itself—the Titans merely keep

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.050
people in line.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.720
They give everyone a common goal.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.300
Now, the  purpose of the Titans is not yet revealed

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:58.780
in the show.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:02.330
We know there is a face in the wall, and that
there are abnormal Titans that are controlled

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:03.330
by people.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:07.140
It could be the case that they are merely
tools of the elite to lower the population--

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:16.640
they could be trying to break people out of their
cages--or they could just be evil.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:21.320
If Annie is in fact working for government
officials to create emergencies and lower

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:26.600
population, if the rogue Titans are in fact
part of an inside conspiracy--then what we

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:32.880
have is a government-fabricated enemy--a threat
that is a Schmitt-ean wet dream--an intelligent,

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:38.720
strong... naked enemy worthy of battle that
will keep humanity from fighting each other..

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:43.860
Also, incidentally if this were the case, it would be a great criticism of Schmitt’s politics.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.610
In a way the Titans could be read as an allegory
for the perfect scapegoat, as the source of

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:54.610
all fears that mobilizes a population and
gives the people in control their very power.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:59.280
Even in the show’s theme of freedom, it reflects Schmitt’s friend-enemy distinction.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.880
The scouts badge is the wings of freedom.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.290
Eren and Armin are constantly crying about
a life beyond the walls.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.960
And humanity is likened to penned in cattle.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:17.300
More than that, freedom and community, for
Schmitt, is defined as denying cowardice in

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:18.980
the face of impending death

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.020
—joining the
scouts is a sort of liberation from the fear

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.380
of living inside the wall waiting to die.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:48.120
The desire to join the scouts together cements
Eren’s class as a community—but not just

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:53.200
any community—a political community that
gives life a purpose...the battlefield.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:03.080
For Schmitt a political community is defined
by the ability to kill your enemies for the

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:07.820
sake of your friends or dying at the hands
of your enemies for the sake your friends.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:11.790
The scouts that risk their lives are like
the troops in the the Alfred Tenyson poem

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.590
“the charge of the light brigade.”

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.060
Yeah Attack on Titan characters’ quote Shakespeare
and Tenyson.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:24.600
Having him quote Tenyson is particularly
prescient-“the Charge of the Light Brigade”

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:29.330
is an exemplar war poem about dying with your
comrades in battle—especially given how

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:31.560
many scouts die fighting Annie.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:36.890
This sense of camaraderie and political community
is what binds together the remnants of humanity,

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:39.300
rather than letting them tear themselves apart.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.960
However, the friend-enemy distinction gets
a little fuzzier as the show progresses.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:49.680
Eren and Annie being Titans erodes the clear
lines between a foreign enemy and a domestic

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.120
friend—it’s why the partial transformation
scene: when Eren saves Mikasa and Armin from

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.100
cannon fire, is essential.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:04.690
It shows what happens when there isn’t a
clear division between human and titan—the

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:09.340
line between who needs to be protected, and
from what, blurs and it makes the task of

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.220
securing the population near impossible.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:17.360
The final element of Schmitt’s, the political,
is the power of the sovereign itself.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:21.780
Sovereign entities have the ability to declare
states of emergencies that justify sacrificing

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:26.500
populations for the greater good—like sending
a battalion to reclaim wall Maria.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:44.620
The ability to declare this kind of state
of emergency is crucial for the long-term

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:48.960
stability of most societies: you don’t want
political bickering getting in the way of

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:52.280
fighting the giant monster about to murder
you all.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:57.110
The sovereign can also make exceptions in
the law—like special citizen status for

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:59.110
the people to live inside wall Sina.

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:03.440
In Attack on Titan we don’t have a very
good explanation of how the political works

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:07.970
outside of the military--it appears that the
current leadership structure is based on marshall

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.520
law and military rule.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.660
Sure, we know that Premiere Dhalis Zachary
is in charge of the military tribunal that

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:17.870
has the power to execute Eren—and we know
that the wall cultists have grown in power

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:27.280
since the attack on Shiganshina—but the
actual structure outside of military control

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:29.160
hasn’t been revealed.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:33.750
We do know that the leaders send millions
to their death to ensure the safety of the

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:36.130
rest of the people inside the walls.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:41.680
Pixus explains that the retaking of wall Maria
was little more than a thinly disguised purge

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:47.040
to ease the stress from the massive influx
of refugees--it was a decision to kill off

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.260
part of the population for the greater good.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:03.720
As twisted as it sounds, for Schmitt, the
sovereign must maintain this ability to do

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:07.650
even the most horrendous of things if order
is to be maintained.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:12.700
So wisecrack—with this in mind, I invite
you to ponder this: what would happen if all

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.800
the Titans suddenly disappeared?

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.020
Would society devolve into anarchy?

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:21.710
Would there be a civil war inside the walls
that would be even more brutal than the occasional

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:22.810
Titan attack?

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:26.490
Or would it be an opportunity for liberation
and greater peace?

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:30.800
For Schmitt eradicating your enemy isn’t
an option because there is always a drive

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:34.330
for warfare, another enemy to be found.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:38.350
Eliminate one enemy and another one pops up
until there are no people left to kill but

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:40.110
your own population.

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:44.800
Of course, we should be wary of a guy who
warned about unending war while being a principal

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.660
theorist for the Nazi Party.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:51.990
There is still a pretty robust debate in academia
about the redeemability and use of Schmitt’s

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:54.820
work for understanding international conflict.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:58.930
People still invoke Schmitt when discussing
executive power, the pitfalls of our current

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:01.270
system, and even the war on terror.

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.480
Attack on Titan could go in so many directions.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:08.360
It could reverse course and become a scathing
criticism of Schmitt style politics, or it

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:09.990
could simply complicate them.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.880
we’ll just have til season two to find out!

